{
  "_about": "Ingredient rules used by check_recipe.py. 'avoid' terms make a recipe fail a diet; 'limit' terms produce portion warnings. 'safe_phrases' are removed from an ingredient name before matching (e.g. 'peanut butter' is not dairy butter). 'neutralizers' mark the whole ingredient as compliant (e.g. anything labelled 'gluten-free'). Matching is case-insensitive and on whole words. A 'limit' group may list 'unless' phrases that exempt it (e.g. almond milk is not a portion of almonds).",
